{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>אך</b> — It limits the effectiveness of rebuke against a rebellious man, for it is of no avail against him. And it is deficient, like איש מרי (a rebellious man). שמרה (he is set on it): for he seeks to do evil to himself." "<b>אכזרי</b> — that he will not have compassion on him." "<b>ישולח בו</b> — to put him to death."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {0 "The reading of the final clause is uncertain; translated hyper-literally. The subject of 'seeks to do evil' is ambiguous and the syntax may be corrupt."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:21.390215583Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}